            "speaker": "B",
            "text": "We are almost finished with the project."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "text": "Has every team finished?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "B",
            "text": "Each team has completed its main task, but we still have little time."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "text": "Are there many issues?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "B",
            "text": "There are a few small issues, and each of them needs attention."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "text": "Do we have enough information?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "B",
            "text": "We don't have enough information from the client, so we may need another meeting."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "text": "Which option is better?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "B",
            "text": "Both options are possible, but neither solution is perfect."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          "Are they finished?",
          "Do they have much time?",
          "Do they need another meeting?"
        ],
        "answers": "1. Almost. 2. Little time. 3. Yes.",
        "note": "almost = nearly done. a few = some, enough to mention. neither = not A and not B."
      },
